<title>NEW ZEALAND: St Lukes looks at Riccarton Mall - paper.</title>
<headline>St Lukes looks at Riccarton Mall - paper.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>St Lukes Group is seeking to add Christchurch's Riccarton Mall to its stable of property investments, the New Zealand Herald said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Herald said it understood the shopping mall owner was looking to pay NZ$100 milion for a 50 percent stake in the country's third largest shoppping centre.</p>
<p>A sale was possible by the end of the year, it said.</p>
<p>Prudential New Zealand and Prudential Australia each own 50 percent of the mall.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
